# Nuvé Project — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Nuvé is a premium food delivery platform. This is a pnpm monorepo.
- app/         → User-facing frontend (Nuxt 3, Vue 3, Tailwind, GSAP)
- admin/       → Staff/Admin dashboard (Nuxt 3, Vue 3, Tailwind)
- server/      → Backend REST API (Fastify, Prisma, PostgreSQL)
- packages/shared/ → Shared TypeScript types used across all workspaces

## Brand
- Primary color: #3DBA7A (Nuvé green)
- Dark theme: backgrounds #080808 / #101010 / #191919
- Fonts: DM Serif Display (headings), DM Sans (UI/body)
- Admin dashboard uses a LIGHT theme — clean, data-dense, professional

## Tech Decisions (never deviate from these)
- Runtime: Node.js 18+, pnpm workspaces
- Backend: Fastify + @fastify/cors + @fastify/jwt + Prisma ORM + PostgreSQL
- Auth: JWT (access token 15min + refresh token 7d stored in httpOnly cookie)
- Passwords: bcrypt (saltRounds: 12)
- Validation: Zod on all request bodies
- Admin UI: Nuxt 3, Tailwind, @headlessui/vue, @vueuse/core, Pinia, recharts via vue-chartjs
- Shared types: packages/shared/types/ — imported as @nuве/shared in both admin and server

## Code Style
- TypeScript everywhere. No implicit any.
- Vue: always <script setup lang="ts">
- Async/await only — no .then() chains
- Prisma: never use raw SQL unless explicitly asked
- API responses always: { success: boolean, data?: T, error?: string, message?: string }
- All Fastify routes have explicit Zod schema validation via fastify-zod or @fastify/type-provider-zod
- No console.log in production code — use Fastify's built-in logger (request.log.info)

## File naming
- Components: PascalCase.vue
- Composables: useXxx.ts
- Stores: xxxStore.ts (Pinia)
- API routes: kebab-case (e.g. /api/restaurants/:id)
- Prisma models: PascalCase singular (Restaurant, Order, User)

## Do not
- Use Express (Fastify only)
- Use any UI component library other than headlessui on admin side
- Use localStorage for auth tokens (httpOnly cookies only)
- Generate placeholder/TODO comments — write real, complete code
- Use default Prisma SQLite in production config — always PostgreSQL